Map data and tiles
------------------

The map at /by-location renders vector tiles built by the pipeline in tiles/
and served from /tiles. Those tiles carry their own attribution,
which the map displays: map data is © OpenStreetMap contributors under the
Open Database License, the tile schema is OpenMapTiles', and the basemap
styles are CARTO's Voyager and Dark Matter (BSD-3-Clause for the style code,
CC-BY 4.0 for the design). No CARTO service is used — the styles are rendered
against our own tiles.

    https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
    https://openmaptiles.org/
    https://carto.com/

Map renderer
------------

The map page loads MapLibre GL JS and the PMTiles protocol shim from
public/map/vendor/, copied out of node_modules at build time by
scripts/copy-map-vendor.mjs. Both are licensed BSD-3-Clause; MapLibre's license
travels with it as public/map/vendor/maplibre-gl-LICENSE.txt.

    https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-gl-js
    https://github.com/protomaps/PMTiles

Display typeface
----------------

The e-ink panel glyphs committed in src/lib/display/atlas.ts are bitmaps
rendered from Lato, by Łukasz Dziedzic, which is licensed under the SIL Open
Font License, Version 1.1:

    https://www.latofonts.com/

Only rasterized output is reproduced — the atlas holds thresholded 1-bit
bitmaps of individual glyphs at five fixed sizes, produced by
scripts/build-font-atlas.mjs. No part of the font software itself is
redistributed, and the atlas is not offered as a font.

One substitution is made: U+21E8, which Lato has no glyph for, is drawn with
Lato's own U+2192 rather than borrowed from another face.
